fix(automations): address CodeRabbit on PR #25

- engine: conditionsPass now fails CLOSED on a malformed condition entry
  (was failing open -> could widen a rule and create unintended tasks).
- engine: per-rule try/catch in runAutomations so one failing rule no longer
  aborts the remaining rules; the failure is logged with the rule id.
- actions: parseJson fails CLOSED on malformed triggerConfig/conditions JSON
  (returns an error instead of a silent broad rule) + validates dueInDays.
- UI: handleToggle/handleDelete now surface { error } results (page-level
  error banner) instead of always refreshing as if successful.
- tests: +4 db-mocked runAutomations orchestrator tests (failure isolation,
  trigger-config matching, condition skip, query-failure safety). 96 total.

Skipped CodeRabbit's "hard-coded TENANT_ID = 1" findings: that is the app-wide
pattern (single-tenant Controllabor); request-scoped tenant context is a
dedicated platform-foundation item (ADR/002 #1), out of scope for this PR.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
